<UserControl x:Class="ConditioningControlPanel.Views.Tabs.PlayTabView"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:helpers="clr-namespace:ConditioningControlPanel.Helpers"
             xmlns:fx="clr-namespace:ConditioningControlPanel.Controls"
             xmlns:loc="clr-namespace:ConditioningControlPanel.Localization"
             xmlns:local="clr-namespace:ConditioningControlPanel"
             mc:Ignorable="d"
             d:DesignHeight="450" d:DesignWidth="800">
    <!--
        ============================ THE PLAY DOOR (tab key "play") ============================
        Phase 6 of the UX restructure, relaid out 2026-08-12. The page frame, the zone rules, the
        one ambient loop, the shared card/lockband style vocabulary, and one card per named Slot*
        Grid. It owns NO feature logic: every click is a one-line shim in PlayTabView.Cards.cs, and
        everything live on the wall (lockbands, the intake's four pass states, the Goon perk line)
        is painted by MainWindow.PlayTab.cs.

        =======================================================================================
        2026-08-12 RELAYOUT. Five entries were removed from THIS PAGE ONLY - Mantras, Available
        Subjects, Deeper, Inspection Bureau and Showcase. Every one of those features is still
        built, still shipped and still reachable by its own door / rail entry / dashboard tile;
        only the duplicate Play-page card is gone. Their handlers survive untouched in MainWindow
        (BtnStartBureau_Click, BtnDeeper_Click, BtnAvailableSubjects_Click, ShowTab("exclusives"),
        StartMantraSession) so nothing else on the surface loses a launch path. Do NOT "restore"
        them here: two doors to one feature is what the restructure exists to stop.

        What is left is nine cards, and the wall is now shaped for nine rather than fourteen:

            HERO      full width   Down the Rabbit Hole            (art: features/dtrh.png)
            TOGETHER  2 columns    Goon Game | Remote Control
            EYES      3 columns    Gaze | Focus Gaze | Blink Trainer   (+ the webcam chip)
            SESSIONS  3 columns    Graded Intake | For You | Lockdown Mode
            MORE      full strip   Loom                            (art: features/loom.png)

        Two deliberate moves in that shape:
          * Blink Trainer moved out of SESSIONS into EYES. It is a WEBCAM feature ("your webcam
            is counting" is its own blurb), so it belongs under the one webcam status chip with
            the other two trackers instead of next to a quiz.
          * The RITUAL zone is dissolved. It held Mantras, Lockdown and Deeper; with two of the
            three gone a zone rule over one card is a header with nothing to head, so Lockdown
            joins SESSIONS (set a timer, hand over the keys - it IS a session) and the loc key
            rf_play_zone_ritual is simply left unused rather than deleted from nine files.

        Every card now uses the SAME art plate (PlayCardArtPlate, 138px) and the SAME four-row
        body - art / title / blurb / call-to-action - with the blurb row taking the slack so the
        buttons line up along the bottom of a row no matter how long a translation runs. That
        bottom alignment is the whole reason the card bodies are Grids and not StackPanels; do not
        flatten them back.

        The Slot* Grids stay: they are the seam a later card is added at, and the reason three
        agents could build this door without ever sharing a file. Card markup goes inside the
        matching <Grid x:Name="Slot*">, shims go in a partial of their own
        (Views\Tabs\PlayTabView.<Area>.cs), never in PlayTabView.xaml.cs. Same convention as
        AppSettingsTabView (Phase 2) and StudioTabView (Phase 4).

        Launch parity is the whole point of the slots. A card's button calls the SAME MainWindow
        handler the old Lab button called, through a one-line shim
        (`if (Window.GetWindow(this) is MainWindow mw) mw.<Handler>(sender, e);`). Nothing on this
        surface may re-implement a launch.

        NO SMOKESCREEN. The Lab tab gated itself with one overlay over the whole page; this door
        mixes free (Goon join), Tier 1 (Lockdown, Blink Trainer, For You, Remote Control) and
        Tier 2 (Rabbit Hole, Gaze, Focus Gaze) in one wall, so the gate is PER CARD: a lockband
        (below) over the art, and the real refusal in the handler via TierGate. The band is
        decoration - IsHitTestVisible=False - so a locked click still reaches the handler and
        still raises the "See tiers" toast.
    -->
    <Grid>
        <Grid.Resources>
            <!-- ==================================================================
                 Card vocabulary. Mod-aware by construction: every colour is a
                 DynamicResource theme key, so the whole wall recolours with the
                 active mod (drone -> green, Bambi -> pink, ...). Carried over from
                 the Lab's LabCard/LabZoneTag/LabCardTitle so a moved card keeps the
                 exact metrics it was authored against - the 9px Margin in
                 particular IS the hover headroom (fx-inventory §12.8: measure with
                 UIA, never eyeball).
                 ================================================================== -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayCard" TargetType="Border">
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="16"/>
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource SurfaceBgBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource PanelAccentBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="22"/>
                <Setter Property="Margin" Value="9"/>
                <Style.Triggers>
                    <Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
                        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource PanelAccentHoverBrush}"/>
                    </Trigger>
                </Style.Triggers>
            </Style>
            <!-- Tier livery variants: a tiered card wears its tier's metal PERMANENTLY -
                 gold = Tier 1, diamond = Tier 2 (Resources\Theme\Brushes.xaml) - so the
                 wall reads free/T1/T2 at a glance even for an account that owns everything
                 (the lockbands below only exist while locked). Own hover triggers, because
                 a derived style's trigger outranks the base one: hover brightens the metal
                 instead of falling back to the mod accent. -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayCardT1" TargetType="Border" BasedOn="{StaticResource PlayCard}">
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource Tier1GoldBorderBrush}"/>
                <Style.Triggers>
                    <Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
                        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource Tier1GoldHoverBrush}"/>
                    </Trigger>
                </Style.Triggers>
            </Style>
            <Style x:Key="PlayCardT2" TargetType="Border" BasedOn="{StaticResource PlayCard}">
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource Tier2DiamondBorderBrush}"/>
                <Style.Triggers>
                    <Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
                        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource Tier2DiamondHoverBrush}"/>
                    </Trigger>
                </Style.Triggers>
            </Style>
            <!-- The art plate every card header sits in. ONE height (138) for the whole wall now
                 that the wall is uniform - the old page ran 132 in three zones and 138 in one,
                 which read as a mistake in a row that mixed them. The negative margin cancels
                 PlayCard's 22px Padding on three sides so the art is full-bleed to the card's
                 rounded top, and the 16 leaves the gap before the title.
                 A card that overrides Height (the wide TOGETHER pair) overrides ONLY Height. -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayCardArtPlate" TargetType="Border">
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="16,16,0,0"/>
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="138"/>
                <Setter Property="Margin" Value="-22,-22,-22,16"/>
                <Setter Property="ClipToBounds" Value="True"/>
            </Style>
            <Style x:Key="PlayZoneTag" TargetType="TextBlock">
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold"/>
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
                <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,14,0"/>
            </Style>
            <!-- The hairline that trails off to the right of a zone tag. Geometry only: the
                 gradient stays INLINE on each Border (the same markup the Lab tab used), because
                 a Freezable carrying a DynamicResource is not a shape this codebase proves out
                 inside a Style setter value. Four copies of four lines beats one clever one. -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayZoneRule" TargetType="Border">
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="1"/>
                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
            </Style>
            <Style x:Key="PlayCardTitle" TargetType="TextBlock">
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextLightBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold"/>
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="18"/>
                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
            </Style>
            <Style x:Key="PlayCardBlurb" TargetType="TextBlock">
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMutedBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12.5"/>
                <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap"/>
                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Top"/>
            </Style>
            <!-- NEW / BETA / SOON chip. Mod-tinted, unlike the lock vocabulary below. -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayBadgePill" TargetType="Border">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource TransparentPink20Brush}"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6"/>
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="6,2"/>
                <Setter Property="Margin" Value="9,0,0,0"/>
                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
            </Style>
            <Style x:Key="PlayBadgePillText" TargetType="TextBlock">
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold"/>
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="9.5"/>
            </Style>
            <!-- The small square emblem plate that sits beside a title. Kept for the two Eyes
                 cards, which carry a glyph next to the name as well as a hero. -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayTitleGlyphPlate" TargetType="Border">
                <Setter Property="Width" Value="34"/>
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="34"/>
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="10"/>
                <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,11,0"/>
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AccentTintedBgBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource PanelAccentBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
            </Style>
            <!-- "Start tracking to play" / "…to enable" and the Bureau-style status pills. -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayStatusPill" TargetType="Border">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AccentTintedBgBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource PanelAccentBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="8"/>
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="10,7"/>
                <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Left"/>
                <Setter Property="Visibility" Value="Collapsed"/>
            </Style>

            <!-- ==================================================================
                 TIER VOCABULARY - deliberately CONSTANT across mods.
                 gold 🔒 = Tier 1, violet 🧪 = Tier 2 (the "Lab" brand survives here,
                 as the badge, and nowhere else). This is a price tag, not decor, so
                 it does NOT take its colour from the mod chain the way the rest of
                 this wall does.

                 These six are a deliberate twin of the rail's RailLock* set
                 (Views\Tabs\SettingsTabView.xaml:364-405), whose own comment says
                 "local to the rail until the Play door adopts the same band, then
                 they belong in the theme". Values are identical to the character.
                 Promoting both sets into Resources\Theme\MainWindow.xaml and
                 deleting the two local copies is a Phase 7/8 cleanup - it touches
                 the rail, which Phase 6 does not own.

                 Band contract, do not break it:
                   * Visibility=Collapsed by default; the painter reveals it.
                   * IsHitTestVisible=False. The card underneath stays live, the
                     click reaches the real handler, and TierGate does the refusing.
                     A band that swallowed the click would be a dead end.
                   * No clock. A lockband is a static state; a Forever loop here
                     would have to be threaded into the motion kill-switch.
                 ================================================================== -->
            <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PlayLockT1Brush" Color="#FFF0C24B"/>
            <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PlayLockT2Brush" Color="#FFB47BFF"/>
            <!-- A scrim, not a curtain: ~66% so the card art still reads through it.
                 Seeing what you are missing is the entire job. -->
            <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PlayLockScrimBrush" Color="#A8120A1E"/>
            <!-- Gold band = Tier 1. CornerRadius matches PlayCard's 16 minus its
                 1px border, so the scrim follows the same inner curve. -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayLockBand" TargetType="Border">
                <Setter Property="Visibility" Value="Collapsed"/>
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="15"/>
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource PlayLockScrimBrush}"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource PlayLockT1Brush}"/>
                <Setter Property="IsHitTestVisible" Value="False"/>
            </Style>
            <!-- Violet band = Tier 2. Two attributes differ, exactly as on the rail. -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayLockBandT2" TargetType="Border" BasedOn="{StaticResource PlayLockBand}">
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource PlayLockT2Brush}"/>
            </Style>
            <!-- TargetType stays TextBlock so it also applies to helpers:EmojiTextBlock
                 (a TextBlock subclass), which is what renders the padlock in colour. -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayLockGlyph" TargetType="TextBlock">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="20"/>
                <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
            </Style>
            <!-- One short line under the glyph. The pitch is the toast the click
                 raises, which carries the "See tiers" button - not this. Trimmed
                 rather than wrapped so a longer translation ends in an ellipsis
                 instead of pushing the band's content out of the card. -->
            <Style x:Key="PlayLockTeaser" TargetType="TextBlock">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold"/>
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource PlayLockT1Brush}"/>
                <Setter Property="TextAlignment" Value="Center"/>
                <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="NoWrap"/>
                <Setter Property="TextTrimming" Value="CharacterEllipsis"/>
                <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
                <Setter Property="Margin" Value="10,6,10,0"/>
            </Style>
            <Style x:Key="PlayLockTeaserT2" TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource PlayLockTeaser}">
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource PlayLockT2Brush}"/>
            </Style>
        </Grid.Resources>

        <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
            <!--
                Entrance stagger note (MainWindow.ChromeFx.cs FindStaggerTargets): the helper
                descends through single-child wrappers and staggers the first panel it finds with
                more than one visible child - which is THIS StackPanel, capped at 6. So the header,
                the hero and the first zone rows stagger in; the cards inside a UniformGrid do not.
                That is the intended reading order. Wrapping a zone in an extra Grid would change
                which elements stagger, so do not "tidy" this tree afterwards.
            -->
            <StackPanel Margin="20">

                <!-- ============================== HEADER ============================== -->
                <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str nav_door_play}" Foreground="White" FontSize="24" FontWeight="Bold"
                           Margin="0,0,0,4">
                    <TextBlock.Effect>
                        <!-- Mod-chain colour. The Lab header hard-coded #00FF88 here, which was the
                             one non-mod-aware literal on that page; it is not carried forward. -->
                        <DropShadowEffect Color="{DynamicResource FxGlowColor}" BlurRadius="20" ShadowDepth="0" Opacity="0.5"/>
                    </TextBlock.Effect>
                </TextBlock>
                <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str pl6_play_subtitle}" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextDimBrush}"
                           FontSize="12" Margin="0,0,0,16"/>

                <!-- ===================== HERO: DOWN THE RABBIT HOLE =====================
                     The frame, the portal gradient, the portal ARTWORK and the ambient loop belong
                     to the host; the title, blurb, FALL IN / Quick Drop buttons and the two Chaos
                     checkboxes go in SlotDtrh. Splitting it that way is what lets the host own the
                     one focal loop on this surface while the cards agent owns every launch.

                     The three-stop gradient is a deliberate portal look, carried over verbatim
                     from the retired LabTabView.xaml:57-61 (deleted in Phase 6; read it with
                     `git show 48a093ebc:ConditioningControlPanel/Views/Tabs/LabTabView.xaml`).
                     It is the one hard-coded palette on this page, and it is still the floor the
                     artwork lays on: if features/dtrh.png ever fails to decode, the hero degrades
                     to exactly the gradient it shipped with rather than to a black hole. -->
                <!-- Diamond frame = Tier 2 livery (Brushes.xaml), same trim as the two Eyes
                     cards, so the wall's most expensive door wears its price openly. -->
                <Border CornerRadius="16" BorderThickness="1" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Tier2DiamondBorderBrush}"
                        Margin="9,0,9,18" ClipToBounds="True" MinHeight="200">
                    <Border.Background>
                        <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,1">
                            <GradientStop Color="#FF2A123A" Offset="0"/>
                            <GradientStop Color="#FF14122A" Offset="0.55"/>
                            <GradientStop Color="#FF3A1030" Offset="1"/>
                        </LinearGradientBrush>
                    </Border.Background>
                    <Grid>
                        <!-- The portal itself. features/dtrh.png is the SAME file the dashboard
                             mosaic's descent tile resolves (MainWindow.Presets.cs:1097
                             "dtrh" => "features/dtrh.png"), so the two surfaces cannot drift and a
                             .ccpmod that reskins the descent reskins this hero with it. Held at
                             just over half opacity and laid UNDER the veil below - it is the room
                             the copy is standing in, never the thing competing with it.
                             Named, and internal, so the mod-art pass in MainWindow.xaml.cs
                             (playHeroMap) can adopt it in place the way it adopts the eight card
                             heroes - it is not in that table yet, which only costs it a repaint on
                             a live mod switch, never correctness. -->
                        <Border Opacity="0.58" IsHitTestVisible="False">
                            <Border.Background>
                                <ImageBrush x:Name="PlayDtrhHeroBrush" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                            ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Resources/features/dtrh.png"
                                            Stretch="UniformToFill" AlignmentY="Center"/>
                            </Border.Background>
                        </Border>
                        <!-- The veil that makes the copy legible over a busy neon illustration:
                             near-opaque under the title and blurb on the left, near-opaque again
                             under the FALL IN column on the right, and open across the middle
                             third, which is exactly where the vortex sits in the art. Tuned to the
                             composition of that PNG - if the art is replaced with something that
                             is not centre-weighted, retune these stops rather than dropping the
                             veil, because the checkbox labels are 11px muted text and they lose
                             every fight with bare artwork. -->
                        <Border IsHitTestVisible="False">
                            <Border.Background>
                                <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                                    <GradientStop Color="#F71A1030" Offset="0"/>
                                    <GradientStop Color="#EC1A1030" Offset="0.42"/>
                                    <GradientStop Color="#571A1030" Offset="0.62"/>
                                    <GradientStop Color="#601A1030" Offset="0.78"/>
                                    <GradientStop Color="#E01A1030" Offset="0.90"/>
                                    <GradientStop Color="#F71A1030" Offset="1"/>
                                </LinearGradientBrush>
                            </Border.Background>
                        </Border>

                        <!-- This door's ONE ambient loop: embers rising behind the portal card.
                             Declared after the art and the veil so the motes drift OVER the
                             illustration (they are the illustration's own dust, not a layer under
                             it), spans the whole card (outside SlotDtrh's margin, so embers reach
                             the card's edges), and is hit-test invisible by construction. Colour
                             comes from FxTheme, so a green Dronification build gets green motes
                             rather than an orange hard-coded into the Play door.

                             Started and registered ONCE by PlayTabView.xaml.cs on first show, as
                             RegisterTabFx("play", ...) - which is both the park/resume hook
                             (SwitchTabFx, MainWindow.AmbientFx.cs) and the motion kill-switch's
                             reach (CmbMotionLevel_SelectionChanged parks every registered canvas
                             with SwitchTabFx("")). The key MUST stay the key ShowTab passes for
                             this view or the canvas runs forever off-screen.

                             No second AmbientFxCanvas may be added to this view: one focal
                             ambient loop per surface (FX_OVERHAUL_PLAN). -->
                        <fx:AmbientFxCanvas x:Name="RabbitHoleFx" x:FieldModifier="internal"/>

                        <Grid x:Name="SlotDtrh" x:FieldModifier="internal" Margin="28,24,28,24">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                                <!-- left: title + blurb. Literal English, carried over verbatim from
                                     the retired LabTabView.xaml:79-93 (deleted in Phase 6; see
                                     git 48a093ebc) - these cards were deliberately never localized
                                     and the move is not the moment to change that. -->
                                <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,8">
                                        <TextBlock Text="🐇 DOWN THE RABBIT HOLE" Foreground="White" FontSize="25" FontWeight="Bold">
                                            <TextBlock.Effect>
                                                <DropShadowEffect Color="{DynamicResource FxGlowColor}" BlurRadius="22" ShadowDepth="0" Opacity="0.7"/>
                                            </TextBlock.Effect>
                                        </TextBlock>
                                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayBadgePill}" Margin="12,2,0,0" Padding="7,2">
                                            <TextBlock Text="NEW" Style="{StaticResource PlayBadgePillText}" FontSize="10"/>
                                        </Border>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                    <TextBlock Text="it's right there. it's always been right there. bubbles drift up carrying flashes, videos, overlays. snap them in time or let them trigger you. stack streaks, accept mantras, sink deeper."
                                               Foreground="{DynamicResource TextLightBrush}" Opacity="0.82" FontSize="13"
                                               TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="480" HorizontalAlignment="Left"/>
                                </StackPanel>

                                <!-- right: launch.
                                     The collapsed Free Desktop / Story radio pair is NOT carried
                                     over, and nothing replaced it. It was already
                                     Visibility=Collapsed on the Lab card (the in-game main menu
                                     owns mode selection), and the seeding its constructor did is
                                     redundant twice over: ChaosModeService.SelectedPlayMode is a
                                     static that already DEFAULTS to FreeDesktop, and StartRun
                                     forces FreeDesktop outright while ChaosModeService
                                     .StoryModeEnabled is false (Services\Chaos\ChaosModeService.cs
                                     - the single reversible switch, false until story content
                                     exists). So deleting LabTabView with its ctor changed nothing.
                                     When Story ships, the picker belongs in ONE place - re-add it
                                     here or leave it to the hub, never both: one setting, one
                                     writer. -->
                                <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="24,0,0,0">
                                    <Button x:Name="BtnPlayFallIn" Content="▶ FALL IN" Cursor="Hand" ToolTip="you were always going to."
                                            Background="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}" Foreground="White" FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="16"
                                            BorderThickness="0" Padding="30,14" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                                            Click="BtnStartChaos_Click">
                                        <Button.Effect>
                                            <DropShadowEffect Color="{DynamicResource FxGlowColor}" BlurRadius="20" ShadowDepth="0" Opacity="0.6"/>
                                        </Button.Effect>
                                        <Button.Resources>
                                            <Style TargetType="Border">
                                                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="14"/>
                                            </Style>
                                        </Button.Resources>
                                    </Button>
                                    <Button x:Name="BtnPlayQuickDrop" Content="💧 Quick Drop" Cursor="Hand"
                                            Background="Transparent" Foreground="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="12"
                                            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}" BorderThickness="1" Padding="14,6" Margin="0,8,0,0"
                                            HorizontalAlignment="Right" ToolTip="skip the dollhouse. fall straight in with your saved settings"
                                            Click="BtnQuickStartChaos_Click">
                                        <Button.Resources>
                                            <Style TargetType="Border">
                                                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="9"/>
                                            </Style>
                                        </Button.Resources>
                                    </Button>
                                    <!-- Pure XAML two-way bindings, portable verbatim: no handler,
                                         no shim, nothing for the move to break.
                                         They ARE named, though: the T2 lockband above is
                                         IsHitTestVisible=False so the FALL IN / Quick Drop refusal
                                         path keeps working, which means these two writers would
                                         otherwise stay clickable straight through the padlock.
                                         RefreshPlayCards disables them with the band.
                                         Foreground is TextLightBrush rather than TextMutedBrush
                                         now that artwork sits behind them - see the veil comment. -->
                                    <CheckBox x:Name="ChkPlayChaosAnnouncer" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                              Content="Announcements"
                                              IsChecked="{Binding Source={x:Static local:App.Settings}, Path=Current.ChaosAnnouncerEnabled, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                              Foreground="{DynamicResource TextLightBrush}" FontSize="11" Cursor="Hand"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Right" Margin="0,12,0,0"
                                              ToolTip="Flash on-screen subtitle announcements (mantra, resistance, depth, streak) during a descent"/>
                                    <CheckBox x:Name="ChkPlayChaosWebGame" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                              Content="3D game (recommended)"
                                              IsChecked="{Binding Source={x:Static local:App.Settings}, Path=Current.ChaosWebGameEnabled, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                              Foreground="{DynamicResource TextLightBrush}" FontSize="11" Cursor="Hand"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Right" Margin="0,6,0,0"
                                              ToolTip="Play inside the 3D rabbit-hole tunnel (browser engine). Untick to use the classic desktop version - e.g. if the 3D one won't start on this machine."/>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </Grid>

                            <!-- The negative margin cancels the slot's own 28,24 inset so the scrim
                                 reaches the hero's edges; 15 is the hero Border's 16 minus its 1px
                                 border, so it follows the same inner curve. Decoration only: the
                                 buttons underneath stay live and TierGate.DemandLab in
                                 BtnStartChaos_Click / BtnQuickStartChaos_Click does the refusing. -->
                            <Border x:Name="PlayLockDtrh" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                    Style="{StaticResource PlayLockBandT2}" Margin="-28,-24,-28,-24">
                                <StackPanel VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <helpers:EmojiTextBlock Text="🧪" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockGlyph}" FontSize="26"/>
                                    <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str hm3_rail_lock_t2}" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockTeaserT2}" FontSize="13"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </Border>
                        </Grid>
                    </Grid>
                </Border>

                <!-- ===================== ZONE: TOGETHER =====================
                     Two cards, and two columns rather than three. Available Subjects was the third
                     entry here and it is gone from this page (still its own tab, still reachable
                     from the rail); leaving Columns="3" behind would have parked a card-shaped hole
                     under the hero. The pair is deliberately WIDE - these are the two "someone else
                     is involved" features, they sit directly under the portal, and a 168px plate on
                     a half-width card keeps the same art-to-copy proportion the 138px plate has on
                     a third-width one. -->
                <Grid Margin="2,4,2,8">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{loc:Str rf_play_zone_together}" Style="{StaticResource PlayZoneTag}"/>
                    <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource PlayZoneRule}">
                        <Border.Background>
                            <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                                <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource PanelAccentHover}" Offset="0"/>
                                <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="1"/>
                            </LinearGradientBrush>
                        </Border.Background>
                    </Border>
                </Grid>
                <!-- Column counts are FIXED on every zone, deliberately: a UniformGrid with an
                     explicit Columns keeps each card the width it was authored at even while a
                     neighbour is hidden. Collapsing to Columns="1" would stretch a hero card
                     across the whole canvas. -->
                <UniformGrid Rows="1" Columns="2">
                    <!-- Goon Game: free to join by design. NO lockband here - the two paid rungs
                         (🔒 send your own media = T1, 🧪 host a room = T2) are named in a sub-line,
                         never a padlock over an open door. See GoonHostService.cs:882-913. -->
                    <Grid x:Name="SlotGoon" x:FieldModifier="internal">
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayCard}">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                    <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                <!-- The duel client's own square wordmark, cropped to the logo with the
                                     ImageBrush Viewbox and laid on the logo's backdrop colour rather
                                     than UniformToFill-cropped like the 16:9 heroes. Carried over
                                     exactly from the retired LabTabView.xaml:198-217 (deleted in
                                     Phase 6; see git 48a093ebc) - Stretch, Viewbox and the
                                     #FF161622 plate are the reason it reads as a wordmark and not as
                                     a smear. Art path never renamed. -->
                                <Border Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardArtPlate}" Height="168"
                                        Background="#FF161622">
                                    <Grid>
                                        <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                            <Border.Background>
                                                <ImageBrush x:Name="PlayGoonHeroBrush" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                            ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Resources/features/goon_game.png"
                                                            Stretch="Uniform" Viewbox="0.03,0.22,0.94,0.68"/>
                                            </Border.Background>
                                        </Border>
                                        <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                            <Border.Background>
                                                <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,1" EndPoint="0,0">
                                                    <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource SurfaceBg}" Offset="0"/>
                                                    <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9"/>
                                                </LinearGradientBrush>
                                            </Border.Background>
                                        </Border>
                                    </Grid>
                                </Border>
                                <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,0,8">
                                    <TextBlock Text="Goon Game" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardTitle}"/>
                                    <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayBadgePill}">
                                        <TextBlock Text="BETA" Style="{StaticResource PlayBadgePillText}"/>
                                    </Border>
                                </StackPanel>
                                <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Text="a 1v1 endurance duel. trade flashes, videos and lock cards in real time. outlast them - or break first."
                                           Style="{StaticResource PlayCardBlurb}" FontSize="12" Margin="0,0,0,14"/>

                                <StackPanel Grid.Row="3">
                                    <!-- NO LOCKBAND, on purpose. Joining is free and deliberately so
                                         (MainWindow.Lab.cs:182-186, GoonHostService.cs:882-913); a
                                         padlock over an open door would be false advertising. The two
                                         paid rungs are NAMED instead, the way the lobby names its
                                         transfer perk rather than greying it out in silence.
                                         RefreshPlayCards dims whichever rung this account has not
                                         bought - it never disables anything, because neither rung is
                                         enforced from this card. -->
                                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Margin="0,0,0,16">
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str pl6_goon_free_to_join}" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextMutedBrush}"
                                                   FontFamily="Consolas" FontSize="10.5" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                        <TextBlock x:Name="TxtPlayGoonPerkSend" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                   Text="{loc:Str pl6_goon_perk_send_t1}" FontFamily="Consolas" FontSize="10.5"
                                                   Foreground="{StaticResource PlayLockT1Brush}" Margin="8,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                        <TextBlock x:Name="TxtPlayGoonPerkHost" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                   Text="{loc:Str pl6_goon_perk_host_t2}" FontFamily="Consolas" FontSize="10.5"
                                                   Foreground="{StaticResource PlayLockT2Brush}" Margin="8,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                    </StackPanel>

                                    <Button x:Name="BtnPlayGoon" Content="Jump In !" Cursor="Hand"
                                            Background="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}" Foreground="White" FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="14"
                                            BorderThickness="0" Padding="30,10" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                            ToolTip="go head to head - first to break loses."
                                            Click="BtnStartGoon_Click">
                                        <Button.Resources>
                                            <Style TargetType="Border"><Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="8"/></Style>
                                        </Button.Resources>
                                    </Button>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </Grid>
                        </Border>
                    </Grid>
                    <Grid x:Name="SlotRemoteControl" x:FieldModifier="internal">
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayCardT1}">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid>
                                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                    <Border Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardArtPlate}" Height="168">
                                        <Grid>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <ImageBrush x:Name="PlayRemoteHeroBrush" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                                ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Resources/features/remote_control.png" Stretch="UniformToFill"/>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,1" EndPoint="0,0">
                                                        <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource SurfaceBg}" Offset="0"/>
                                                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9"/>
                                                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Border>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Text="{loc:Str tab_remote_control}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardTitle}" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Text="{loc:Str pl6_card_blurb_remote}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardBlurb}" Margin="0,0,0,16"/>
                                    <!-- Navigation only. The waiver, the login check and the deferred
                                         revert all live in ChkRemoteControlEnabled_Changed on that
                                         page; a second enable path here would be a second gate. -->
                                    <Button Grid.Row="3" x:Name="BtnPlayRemoteControl" Content="{loc:Str btn_open}" Cursor="Hand"
                                            HorizontalAlignment="Left" Padding="16,8"
                                            Background="{DynamicResource AccentGradientBrush}" Foreground="White"
                                            BorderThickness="0" FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13"
                                            Click="BtnPlayRemoteControl_Click">
                                        <Button.Resources>
                                            <Style TargetType="Border"><Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="10"/></Style>
                                        </Button.Resources>
                                    </Button>
                                </Grid>
                                <Border x:Name="PlayLockRemote" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                        Style="{StaticResource PlayLockBand}" Margin="-22">
                                    <StackPanel VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <helpers:EmojiTextBlock Text="🔒" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockGlyph}"/>
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str hm3_rail_lock_t1}" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockTeaser}"/>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Border>
                            </Grid>
                        </Border>
                    </Grid>
                </UniformGrid>

                <!-- ===================== ZONE: EYES =====================
                     All THREE webcam features, under the one webcam chip. Blink Trainer moved here
                     from SESSIONS on 2026-08-12: its own blurb is "your webcam is counting", so
                     filing it beside a quiz was the page telling a small lie about what it needs. -->
                <Grid Margin="2,18,2,8">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{loc:Str rf_play_zone_eyes}" Style="{StaticResource PlayZoneTag}"/>
                    <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource PlayZoneRule}">
                        <Border.Background>
                            <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                                <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource PanelAccentHover}" Offset="0"/>
                                <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="1"/>
                            </LinearGradientBrush>
                        </Border.Background>
                    </Border>
                </Grid>
                <!-- Read-only webcam status chip. Settings → Devices has owned the camera since
                     Phase 2; the Eyes cards dim against tracker state, so the state has to be
                     visible here - but it is DISPLAY ONLY. Painted by UpdateWebcamStatusChips
                     (MainWindow.LabTab.cs), which paints three surfaces from one method: whoever
                     fills this slot must keep the chip's named parts resolvable or the Blink
                     Trainer and Deeper chips break with it. -->
                <Grid x:Name="SlotWebcamChip" x:FieldModifier="internal">
                    <!-- Three named parts, painted by UpdateWebcamStatusChips (MainWindow.LabTab.cs),
                         which paints THREE surfaces from one method - this chip, the Blink Trainer's
                         and Deeper's. Rename any of these and the other two go with it. -->
                    <Border x:Name="WebcamStatusChipPlay" x:FieldModifier="internal" CornerRadius="14" Margin="9,4,9,12" Padding="16,13"
                            Background="{DynamicResource PanelBgBrush}" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource PanelAccentBrush}" BorderThickness="1">
                        <Grid>
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <Ellipse Grid.Column="0" x:Name="WebcamStatusChipPlayDot" x:FieldModifier="internal" Width="9" Height="9"
                                     Fill="{DynamicResource TextMutedBrush}" Margin="0,0,11,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str set2_webcam_chip_label}" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextLightBrush}"
                                           FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="14"/>
                                <TextBlock x:Name="TxtWebcamStatusChipPlay" x:FieldModifier="internal" Text="{loc:Str rf_webcam_stopped}"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource TextMutedBrush}" FontFamily="Consolas" FontSize="11"/>
                            </StackPanel>
                            <Button Grid.Column="2" Content="{loc:Str set2_configure_in_settings}"
                                    Padding="12,6" VerticalAlignment="Center" Cursor="Hand"
                                    Background="Transparent" Foreground="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}"
                                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}" BorderThickness="1" FontSize="11" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                    Click="BtnOpenDeviceSettings_Click">
                                <Button.Resources><Style TargetType="Border"><Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="8"/></Style></Button.Resources>
                            </Button>
                        </Grid>
                    </Border>
                </Grid>
                <UniformGrid Rows="1" Columns="3">
                    <Grid x:Name="SlotGaze" x:FieldModifier="internal">
                        <!-- PlayGazeCard / PlayGazeNeedsTracker are written by UpdateLabTrackerUi
                             (Opacity 1.0 / 0.62 + the "start tracking" band) off the tracker-state
                             event. Tracker dimming and the tier band are two independent states and
                             they stack: an unentitled account with the camera off sees both. -->
                        <Border x:Name="PlayGazeCard" x:FieldModifier="internal" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardT2}">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid>
                                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                    <Border Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardArtPlate}">
                                        <Grid>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <ImageBrush x:Name="PlayGazeHeroBrush" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                                ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Resources/features/lab_gaze_hero.png" Stretch="UniformToFill"/>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,1" EndPoint="0,0">
                                                        <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource SurfaceBg}" Offset="0"/>
                                                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9"/>
                                                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Border>
                                    <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,0,6">
                                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayTitleGlyphPlate}">
                                            <Image Width="18" Height="18" Source="{Binding Source='🎯', Converter={StaticResource EmojiToImageSource}}"/>
                                        </Border>
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str label_gaze_minigame}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardTitle}"/>
                                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayBadgePill}">
                                            <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str label_beta_2}" Style="{StaticResource PlayBadgePillText}"/>
                                        </Border>
                                        <!-- Same registry entry ("GazeMinigame"), same popover - only the
                                             accessor path in MainWindow.Presets.cs changes. -->
                                        <Button x:Name="HelpBtnPlayGazeMinigame" x:FieldModifier="internal" Style="{StaticResource HelpButtonStyle}"
                                                Tag="GazeMinigame" Margin="6,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Text="{loc:Str label_gaze_minigame_description}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardBlurb}" Margin="0,0,0,14"/>
                                    <StackPanel Grid.Row="3">
                                        <Button x:Name="BtnPlayGazeMinigame" Content="{loc:Str btn_open}"
                                                ToolTip="{loc:Str tooltip_gaze_minigame_open}" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                                Padding="16,8" Background="{DynamicResource AccentGradientBrush}" Foreground="White"
                                                BorderThickness="0" FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13" Cursor="Hand"
                                                Click="BtnGazeMinigame_Click">
                                            <Button.Resources>
                                                <Style TargetType="Border"><Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="10"/></Style>
                                            </Button.Resources>
                                        </Button>
                                        <Border x:Name="PlayGazeNeedsTracker" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                Style="{StaticResource PlayStatusPill}" Margin="0,12,0,0">
                                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                                <Ellipse Width="7" Height="7" Fill="{DynamicResource TextMutedBrush}" Margin="0,0,8,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                                <TextBlock Text="Start tracking to play" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextMutedBrush}" FontFamily="Consolas" FontSize="11" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                            </StackPanel>
                                        </Border>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Grid>
                                <Border x:Name="PlayLockGaze" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                        Style="{StaticResource PlayLockBandT2}" Margin="-22">
                                    <StackPanel VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <helpers:EmojiTextBlock Text="🧪" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockGlyph}"/>
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str hm3_rail_lock_t2}" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockTeaserT2}"/>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Border>
                            </Grid>
                        </Border>
                    </Grid>
                    <!-- Focus Gaze is a separate card from the Gaze Minigame (separate handler,
                         separate art, separate needs-tracker band). It is NOT part of SlotGaze. -->
                    <Grid x:Name="SlotFocusGaze" x:FieldModifier="internal">
                        <Border x:Name="PlayFocusCard" x:FieldModifier="internal" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardT2}">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid>
                                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                    <Border Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardArtPlate}">
                                        <Grid>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <ImageBrush x:Name="PlayFocusHeroBrush" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                                ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Resources/features/lab_focusgaze_hero.png" Stretch="UniformToFill"/>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,1" EndPoint="0,0">
                                                        <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource SurfaceBg}" Offset="0"/>
                                                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9"/>
                                                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Border>
                                    <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,0,6">
                                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayTitleGlyphPlate}">
                                            <Image Width="18" Height="18" Source="{Binding Source='✨', Converter={StaticResource EmojiToImageSource}}"/>
                                        </Border>
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str label_focus_gaze}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardTitle}"/>
                                        <Button x:Name="HelpBtnPlayFocusGaze" x:FieldModifier="internal" Style="{StaticResource HelpButtonStyle}"
                                                Tag="FocusGaze" Margin="6,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Text="{loc:Str label_focus_gaze_description}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardBlurb}" Margin="0,0,0,12"/>
                                    <StackPanel Grid.Row="3">
                                        <Grid>
                                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{loc:Str btn_enable}" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextLightBrush}" FontSize="14" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                            <!-- The ONE Focus Gaze switch. ChkFocusGaze_Changed reads this
                                                 control and writes TxtPlayFocusGazeStatus below; the Lab
                                                 copies it used to read are dead with that view. -->
                                            <CheckBox Grid.Column="1" x:Name="ChkPlayFocusGaze" x:FieldModifier="internal" Style="{StaticResource ToggleStyle}"
                                                      ToolTip="{loc:Str tooltip_focus_gaze_toggle}" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                      Checked="ChkFocusGaze_Changed" Unchecked="ChkFocusGaze_Changed"/>
                                        </Grid>
                                        <TextBlock x:Name="TxtPlayFocusGazeStatus" x:FieldModifier="internal" Text=""
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource SuccessGreenBrush}" FontSize="11" Margin="0,6,0,0"
                                                   TextWrapping="Wrap"/>
                                        <Border x:Name="PlayFocusNeedsTracker" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                Style="{StaticResource PlayStatusPill}" Margin="0,12,0,0">
                                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                                <Ellipse Width="7" Height="7" Fill="{DynamicResource TextMutedBrush}" Margin="0,0,8,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                                <TextBlock Text="Start tracking to enable" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextMutedBrush}" FontFamily="Consolas" FontSize="11" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                            </StackPanel>
                                        </Border>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Grid>
                                <Border x:Name="PlayLockFocusGaze" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                        Style="{StaticResource PlayLockBandT2}" Margin="-22">
                                    <StackPanel VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <helpers:EmojiTextBlock Text="🧪" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockGlyph}"/>
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str hm3_rail_lock_t2}" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockTeaserT2}"/>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Border>
                            </Grid>
                        </Border>
                    </Grid>
                    <!-- Blink Trainer: an EYES card since the 2026-08-12 relayout. Tier 1, and it
                         keeps its own page's gate - this card only navigates. It does NOT take the
                         tracker-dimming treatment the two cards beside it do: PlayGazeCard /
                         PlayFocusCard are dimmed by UpdateLabTrackerUi because their features need
                         a LIVE tracker to be playable at all, whereas the Blink Trainer page starts
                         its own camera. Adding it to that method would be a behaviour change in
                         MainWindow.LabTab.cs, which this relayout does not touch. -->
                    <Grid x:Name="SlotBlinkTrainer" x:FieldModifier="internal">
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayCardT1}">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid>
                                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                    <Border Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardArtPlate}">
                                        <Grid>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <ImageBrush x:Name="PlayBlinkHeroBrush" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                                ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Resources/features/blink_trainer.png" Stretch="UniformToFill"/>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,1" EndPoint="0,0">
                                                        <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource SurfaceBg}" Offset="0"/>
                                                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9"/>
                                                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Border>
                                    <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,0,6">
                                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayTitleGlyphPlate}">
                                            <Image Width="18" Height="18" Source="{Binding Source='👁', Converter={StaticResource EmojiToImageSource}}"/>
                                        </Border>
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str tab_blink_trainer}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardTitle}"/>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Text="{loc:Str pl6_card_blurb_blink}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardBlurb}" Margin="0,0,0,16"/>
                                    <Button Grid.Row="3" x:Name="BtnPlayBlinkTrainer" Content="{loc:Str btn_open}" Cursor="Hand"
                                            HorizontalAlignment="Left" Padding="16,8"
                                            Background="{DynamicResource AccentGradientBrush}" Foreground="White"
                                            BorderThickness="0" FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13"
                                            Click="BtnLabBlinkTrainerOpenNew_Click">
                                        <Button.Resources>
                                            <Style TargetType="Border"><Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="10"/></Style>
                                        </Button.Resources>
                                    </Button>
                                </Grid>
                                <Border x:Name="PlayLockBlink" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                        Style="{StaticResource PlayLockBand}" Margin="-22">
                                    <StackPanel VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <helpers:EmojiTextBlock Text="🔒" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockGlyph}"/>
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str hm3_rail_lock_t1}" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockTeaser}"/>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Border>
                            </Grid>
                        </Border>
                    </Grid>
                </UniformGrid>

                <!-- ===================== ZONE: SESSIONS =====================
                     Three ways to commit to a run: sit the evaluation, scroll until you can't, or
                     hand over the keys on a timer. Lockdown Mode arrived here on 2026-08-12 when
                     the RITUAL zone was dissolved (its other two cards, Mantras and Deeper, left
                     this page); it is a timed session and it reads as one next to these two. -->
                <Grid Margin="2,18,2,8">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{loc:Str rf_play_zone_sessions}" Style="{StaticResource PlayZoneTag}"/>
                    <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource PlayZoneRule}">
                        <Border.Background>
                            <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                                <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource PanelAccentHover}" Offset="0"/>
                                <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="1"/>
                            </LinearGradientBrush>
                        </Border.Background>
                    </Border>
                </Grid>
                <UniformGrid Rows="1" Columns="3">
                    <!-- Four gate states, not two (Premium / Available / Spent / NeedsLogin). The
                         card carries the band; the PAGE keeps RefreshGradedIntakeGate and the
                         launch. Every state navigates to ShowTab("gradedintake") - a Spent user
                         has to be able to read why. -->
                    <Grid x:Name="SlotGradedIntake" x:FieldModifier="internal">
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayCard}">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid>
                                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                    <Border Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardArtPlate}">
                                        <Grid>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <ImageBrush x:Name="PlayIntakeHeroBrush" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                                ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Resources/features/lab_quiz_hero.png" Stretch="UniformToFill"/>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,1" EndPoint="0,0">
                                                        <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource SurfaceBg}" Offset="0"/>
                                                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9"/>
                                                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Border>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Text="{loc:Str tab_gradedintake}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardTitle}" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Text="{loc:Str pl6_card_blurb_intake}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardBlurb}" Margin="0,0,0,10"/>
                                    <StackPanel Grid.Row="3">
                                        <!-- The state line: written by RefreshPlayCards from the SAME
                                             IntakePassService.State that RefreshGradedIntakeGate reads,
                                             so the card and the page can never disagree about the week.
                                             Premium sees nothing here at all - patrons must never learn
                                             the free weekly pass exists. -->
                                        <TextBlock x:Name="TxtPlayIntakeState" x:FieldModifier="internal" Text=""
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}" FontFamily="Consolas" FontSize="11"
                                                   TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,12" Visibility="Collapsed"/>
                                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                                            <!-- Every state navigates. A Spent user has to be able to
                                                 READ why, and the page's four-state gate is the thing
                                                 that says it; refusing the click here would hide the
                                                 explanation. -->
                                            <Button x:Name="BtnPlayGradedIntake" Content="{loc:Str btn_open}" Cursor="Hand"
                                                    Padding="16,8" Background="{DynamicResource AccentGradientBrush}" Foreground="White"
                                                    BorderThickness="0" FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13"
                                                    Click="BtnPlayGradedIntake_Click">
                                                <Button.Resources>
                                                    <Style TargetType="Border"><Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="10"/></Style>
                                                </Button.Resources>
                                            </Button>
                                            <!-- The pass is handed out by the Home logo tile's flip
                                                 ceremony, so "where do I get one" has exactly one honest
                                                 answer: Home. Shown only in the Available state. -->
                                            <Button x:Name="BtnPlayIntakePassHome" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                    Content="{loc:Str pl6_intake_pass_home}" Cursor="Hand" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                                    Margin="10,0,0,0" Padding="14,8" Background="Transparent"
                                                    Foreground="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}"
                                                    BorderThickness="1" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="12"
                                                    Click="BtnPlayIntakePassHome_Click">
                                                <Button.Resources>
                                                    <Style TargetType="Border"><Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="9"/></Style>
                                                </Button.Resources>
                                            </Button>
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Grid>
                                <!-- Gold, and the "Weekly pass" teaser rather than "Patron only":
                                     this is not a tier question. A free account holding this week's
                                     pass is entitled, and RefreshPlayCards reads the pass, not the
                                     tier - exactly what the dashboard rail's LockBandIntake does. -->
                                <Border x:Name="PlayLockIntake" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                        Style="{StaticResource PlayLockBand}" Margin="-22">
                                    <StackPanel VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <helpers:EmojiTextBlock Text="🔒" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockGlyph}"/>
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str hm3_rail_lock_pass}" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockTeaser}"/>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Border>
                            </Grid>
                        </Border>
                    </Grid>
                    <!-- For You is a window, not a tab: the card must call ShowTab("fyp"), which
                         ShowTab intercepts into OpenFypFeed (the shared, gated launch path).
                         Never call FypHostService.Launch() from here. -->
                    <Grid x:Name="SlotFyp" x:FieldModifier="internal">
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayCardT1}">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid>
                                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                    <Border Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardArtPlate}">
                                        <Grid>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <ImageBrush x:Name="PlayFypHeroBrush" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                                ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Resources/features/fyp.png" Stretch="UniformToFill"/>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,1" EndPoint="0,0">
                                                        <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource SurfaceBg}" Offset="0"/>
                                                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9"/>
                                                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Border>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Text="{loc:Str tab_fyp}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardTitle}" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Text="{loc:Str pl6_card_blurb_fyp}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardBlurb}" Margin="0,0,0,16"/>
                                    <!-- ShowTab("fyp"), never FypHostService.Launch(): ShowTab
                                         intercepts that key into OpenFypFeed, which owns the premium
                                         gate and is the same launch path the dashboard chip uses. -->
                                    <Button Grid.Row="3" x:Name="BtnPlayFyp" Content="{loc:Str btn_open}" Cursor="Hand"
                                            HorizontalAlignment="Left" Padding="16,8"
                                            Background="{DynamicResource AccentGradientBrush}" Foreground="White"
                                            BorderThickness="0" FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13"
                                            Click="BtnPlayFyp_Click">
                                        <Button.Resources>
                                            <Style TargetType="Border"><Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="10"/></Style>
                                        </Button.Resources>
                                    </Button>
                                </Grid>
                                <Border x:Name="PlayLockFyp" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                        Style="{StaticResource PlayLockBand}" Margin="-22">
                                    <StackPanel VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <helpers:EmojiTextBlock Text="🔒" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockGlyph}"/>
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str hm3_rail_lock_t1}" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockTeaser}"/>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Border>
                            </Grid>
                        </Border>
                    </Grid>
                    <!-- Navigates to ShowTab("lockdown"). The activation double-warning and
                         App.Lockdown.Activate stay on that page; nothing here re-implements them.
                         The lockdown pulse is that page's, and Phase 6 does not touch it. -->
                    <Grid x:Name="SlotLockdown" x:FieldModifier="internal">
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayCardT1}">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid>
                                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                    <!-- lockdown_icon.png lives at the RESOURCE ROOT, not under
                                         features/ - that is the path mods key against and it is
                                         never "tidied" into the folder its neighbours use. -->
                                    <Border Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardArtPlate}">
                                        <Grid>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <ImageBrush x:Name="PlayLockdownHeroBrush" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                                ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Resources/lockdown_icon.png" Stretch="UniformToFill"/>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                            <Border CornerRadius="16,16,0,0">
                                                <Border.Background>
                                                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,1" EndPoint="0,0">
                                                        <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource SurfaceBg}" Offset="0"/>
                                                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9"/>
                                                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                                                </Border.Background>
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Border>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Text="{loc:Str tab_lockdown_mode}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardTitle}" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Text="{loc:Str pl6_card_blurb_lockdown}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardBlurb}" Margin="0,0,0,16"/>
                                    <!-- Navigation only. The duration dial, the double warning and
                                         App.Lockdown.Activate stay on that page - this card must not
                                         be a second way to take someone's keys away for an hour. -->
                                    <Button Grid.Row="3" x:Name="BtnPlayLockdown" Content="{loc:Str btn_open}" Cursor="Hand"
                                            HorizontalAlignment="Left" Padding="16,8"
                                            Background="{DynamicResource AccentGradientBrush}" Foreground="White"
                                            BorderThickness="0" FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13"
                                            Click="BtnPlayLockdown_Click">
                                        <Button.Resources>
                                            <Style TargetType="Border"><Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="10"/></Style>
                                        </Button.Resources>
                                    </Button>
                                </Grid>
                                <Border x:Name="PlayLockLockdown" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                        Style="{StaticResource PlayLockBand}" Margin="-22">
                                    <StackPanel VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <helpers:EmojiTextBlock Text="🔒" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockGlyph}"/>
                                        <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str hm3_rail_lock_t1}" Style="{StaticResource PlayLockTeaser}"/>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Border>
                            </Grid>
                        </Border>
                    </Grid>
                </UniformGrid>

                <!-- ===================== ZONE: MORE =====================
                     One entry left in this zone (Bureau and Showcase came off the page on
                     2026-08-12), so it is a full-width STRIP rather than a lone third-width card
                     with two empty columns beside it. The strip form is also the honest one for
                     what this row does: Loom is a signpost to another door, not a launch. -->
                <Grid Margin="2,18,2,8">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{loc:Str rf_play_zone_more}" Style="{StaticResource PlayZoneTag}"/>
                    <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource PlayZoneRule}">
                        <Border.Background>
                            <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                                <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource PanelAccentHover}" Offset="0"/>
                                <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="1"/>
                            </LinearGradientBrush>
                        </Border.Background>
                    </Border>
                </Grid>
                <!-- Loom NAVIGATES, it does not launch. Its only entry today is BtnOpenLoom on the
                     Spiral module of the Studio rack (Features\SpiralFeatureControl.xaml:135), and a
                     second Launch() button here would be the duplicate-editor failure the
                     restructure forbids - the same rule that keeps Lockdown, Remote and Blink as
                     navigation cards. So this strip walks the user to the one editor:
                     ShowTab("studio") + FocusRackEntry("spiral"), through OpenStudioModule, which
                     is the path every dashboard mosaic tile uses. (Separately, and out of scope:
                     LoomHostService has no tier check at all - worth a ledger row.) -->
                <Grid x:Name="SlotLoom" x:FieldModifier="internal">
                    <!-- Padding 0 overrides PlayCard's 22 so the art bleeds to the strip's rounded
                         left edge; the copy carries its own inset instead. -->
                    <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayCard}" Padding="0" MinHeight="118">
                        <Grid>
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="216"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <!-- features/loom.png, the same neon-loom plate the feature ships with.
                                 Named + internal so the mod-art pass can adopt it in place later,
                                 exactly like PlayDtrhHeroBrush on the hero. The second Border is the
                                 same bottom-to-top scrim every card hero carries, turned 90° - it
                                 fades the art into SurfaceBg at the copy's edge so a busy
                                 illustration never runs into the title. -->
                            <Border Grid.Column="0" CornerRadius="15,0,0,15" ClipToBounds="True">
                                <Grid>
                                    <Border CornerRadius="15,0,0,15">
                                        <Border.Background>
                                            <ImageBrush x:Name="PlayLoomHeroBrush" x:FieldModifier="internal"
                                                        ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Resources/features/loom.png"
                                                        Stretch="UniformToFill"/>
                                        </Border.Background>
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border CornerRadius="15,0,0,15">
                                        <Border.Background>
                                            <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="1,0" EndPoint="0,0">
                                                <GradientStop Color="{DynamicResource SurfaceBg}" Offset="0"/>
                                                <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.85"/>
                                            </LinearGradientBrush>
                                        </Border.Background>
                                    </Border>
                                </Grid>
                            </Border>
                            <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="4,20,20,20">
                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,6">
                                    <Border Style="{StaticResource PlayTitleGlyphPlate}">
                                        <Image Width="18" Height="18" Source="{Binding Source='🧵', Converter={StaticResource EmojiToImageSource}}"/>
                                    </Border>
                                    <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str pl6_loom_title}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardTitle}"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                                <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str pl6_loom_blurb}" Style="{StaticResource PlayCardBlurb}" MaxWidth="560" HorizontalAlignment="Left"/>
                            </StackPanel>
                            <Button Grid.Column="2" x:Name="BtnPlayLoom" Content="{loc:Str pl6_open_in_studio}" Cursor="Hand"
                                    VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,24,0" Padding="18,9"
                                    Background="Transparent" Foreground="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}"
                                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}" BorderThickness="1" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="12"
                                    Click="BtnPlayLoom_Click">
                                <Button.Resources>
                                    <Style TargetType="Border"><Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="9"/></Style>
                                </Button.Resources>
                            </Button>
                        </Grid>
                    </Border>
                </Grid>

            </StackPanel>
        </ScrollViewer>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
